#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068844 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068451 :question/id #uuid "d53c6172-978d-57c7-b1f0-e56e892e48a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10997" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n    =\n    \\dfrac{x}{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2K \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C= 2K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^2 = x^2 + C .\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564796 :question-generator/id #uuid "2d82efaf-0de8-5ed0-aa7d-bda86ee03de3" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186068844.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06161b70-c2b1-55cf-b1de-7e7405481b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272443} {:answer/id #uuid "39421cbc-ac97-518d-bd42-917038547d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{y}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272887} {:answer/id #uuid "444dd661-b7e1-574e-8d5f-f13ae9f6b31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y}=2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272968